  "pr_number": 442,
  "issue_number": 437,
  "issue_title": "[bug] DROP/BBH graders ignore \\boxed{ANS} while format_hint tells models to box \u2014 correct answers score 0.0",
  "issue_body": "**Describe the bug**\n\n`format_hint(\"drop\")` / BBH instruct models to put the final answer in `\\boxed{}` (via `trinity.fugu.workflow.format_hint`), but `score_drop` / `score_bbh` never peel `\\boxed{...}`. A correct `Answer: \\boxed{21}` becomes token noise (`boxed21` / literal backslash) and scores **0.0**.\n\n**Expected vs actual**\n\n| candidate | gold | expected | actual |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `Answer: \\boxed{21}` (DROP) | `21` | 1.0 | **0.0** |\n| `\\boxed{True}` (BBH exact) | `True` | 1.0 | **0.0** |\n\n`format_hint(\"drop\")` contains `boxed`.\n\n**To reproduce**\n\n```\nPYTHONPATH=src python -c \"\nfrom trinity.adapters.drop import score_drop\nfrom trinity.adapters.bbh import score_bbh\nfrom trinity.fugu.workflow import format_hint\nprint('boxed' in format_hint('drop').lower())  # True\nprint(score_drop(r'Answer: \\boxed{21}', {'gold_answers': ['21']}))  # 0.0  expected 1.0\nprint(score_bbh(r'\\boxed{True}', {'answer': 'True', 'answer_type': 'exact_match'}))  # 0.0  expected 1.0\n\"\n```\n\n- **Benchmarks:** drop, bbh\n- **Affected files:** `src/trinity/adapters/drop.py`, `src/trinity/adapters/bbh.py` (and optionally `format_hint`)\n\n**Suggested fix**\n\nCall `extract_boxed` (last non-empty box) before DROP/BBH normalization when present; leave non-boxed answers unchanged.\n\n**Environment**\n- Python 3.11 (CI) / 3.12 (local)\n- Commit hash: `56c319e`",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-23T11:20:34.000Z",
